context:
PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/workflows/{workflow_name}
Creates a new workflow or updates an existing workflow definition.
Required: workflow_name (path); account_id (path); body (body)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/workflows/{workflow_name}
Deletes a Workflow. This only deletes the Workflow and does not delete or modify any Worker associated to this Workflow or bounded to it.
Required: workflow_name (path); account_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/workflows/{workflow_name}/instances/{instance_id}
Deletes a workflow instance and its stored state.
Required: workflow_name (path); instance_id (path) — Instance identifier. User-created instances match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_][a-zA-Z0-9-_]*$` (max 100 characters); cron-triggered instances can use a longer, system-generated id derived from the cron expression.; account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/workflows/{workflow_name}/versions/{version_id}
Retrieves details for a specific deployed workflow version.
Required: workflow_name (path); version_id (path); account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/workflows/{workflow_name}
Retrieves configuration and metadata for a specific workflow.
Required: workflow_name (path); account_id (path)

POST /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/workflows/{workflow_name}/instances/{instance_id}/events/{event_type}
Sends an event to a running workflow instance to trigger state transitions.
Required: workflow_name (path); instance_id (path) — Instance identifier. User-created instances match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_][a-zA-Z0-9-_]*$` (max 100 characters); cron-triggered instances can use a longer, system-generated id derived from the cron expression.; event_type (path); account_id (path); body (body)
